  "prefLabel": "Env-A 103.28 Foundry",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 103.28 “Foundry” means the equipment used for the processing of metals, including but not limited to handling and preparing raw materials, producing metal molds and cores, and melting, casting and finishing metals.\n\nSource. #6428-A, eff 1-18-97; renumbered by #8256 (from Env-A 101.129), see Revision Note #1 at chapter heading; renumbered by #8304 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading); renumbered by #9839 (from Env-A 101.83), (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading); ss by #13105, eff 9-25-20 (formerly Env-A 101.84) (see Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-A 100)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a100.html"
